EXT. ICE FLOE - ARCTIC DUSK

Gray sky. Wind scours the ice. A tent, flapping. A sled, half-buried.

CAPTAIN LARS HOLMGREN, 50s, wraps a rope around his fist. NURSE ELENI PAPADAKIS, 30s, kneels by a wrapped shape. DEEPAK RAO, 40s, a cook, melts snow in a dented pot. A boy, FINN HOLMGREN, 12, watches the horizon.

LARS
(to all)
Pack it up. We move at first light.

ELENI
(to Lars)
He can't be moved.

LARS
He can't stay.

DEEPAK
(to himself)
Soup. Only soup left. Sure.

Finn slowly turns from the horizon.

FINN
(to Lars)
Dad, the ice is cracking.

LARS
It's always cracking.

FINN
Louder, this time.

Lars glances down at the wrapped shape, then at Eleni. She holds his gaze and gently pulls the blanket over the face. Lars takes off his gloves. Puts them on Finn.

LARS
(quiet, to Finn)
Hold these for me.

He walks to the sled and begins loading it.
